{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e30cafd4d0f6d6bd","name":"card_event_honorifics","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_honorifics","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HONORIFICS","text":"Convert a friendly unit into your last destroyed unit.","flavorText":"During WWII, the Soviet Union used a wide system of honorifics to recognize heroism and exceptional service. The highest individual award was Hero of the Soviet Union, given to people who showed outstanding bravery, either in combat or civilian roles. Recipients got a Gold Star medal and were also awarded the Order of Lenin. Units that performed especially well in battle could be given the Guards title. This raised their status and gave them better equipment, priority in reinforcements, and higher pay. These units often led major offensives. Some cities were honored with the title Hero City for their defense and sacrifice. Cities like Moscow, Leningrad, Stalingrad, and Sevastopol received this title, commemorated with a monument. The Soviet military also gave out many other awards, such as the Order of the Red Banner and service medals. In terms of rank, senior leaders could be named Marshal of the Soviet Union, while Generalissimo was a special title given only to Joseph Stalin. This system helped reward loyalty and boost morale during the war.","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_honorifics","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_honorifics_title","SourceString":"HONORIFICS","LocalizedString":"HONORIFICS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_honorifics_text","SourceString":"Convert a friendly unit into your last destroyed unit.","LocalizedString":"Convert a friendly unit into your last destroyed unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"c